    "title": "Suspect arrested after reported disturbance in Montgomery - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By John Budenas ,\n7 hours ago\nMONTGOMERY, Mass. (WWLP) – A suspect was arrested on Tuesday night following a reported disturbance at a home in Montgomery.\nSpringfield police investigate shooting, arrest two in break-in According to police, local and state officials received information around 6:45 p.m. about a disturbance that occurred earlier in the evening at a residence on Pine Ridge Road.\nAn investigation was launched, and authorities later located the suspect at a residence in Chester. Police say the individual was taken into custody without incident.\nRussell-Montgomery Police thanked the Massachusetts State Police for their assistance. No additional details, including the nature of the disturbance or the identity of the suspect, have been released.\nLocal News Headlines South Hadley police seek public’s help locating missing 25-year-old woman Over 122 million Americans expected to travel during winter holidays Service Above Self luncheon honors community contributions 22News reporter Areta Odiah discusses journalism at Ludlow Senior Center WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Download the 22News Plus app on your TV to watch live-streaming newscasts and video on demand.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WWLP.",
